{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791311177,"nonce":"tRwRTlK6+JADS8Q/TGzC0f8ZgdY=","message":"Quiet NUC, LLVM verified, normal tiering, taskset 0-7, alternating complete processes with independent checksum checks: the initial scalar-adapter prototype improves fast-count SOR wall time 8077 -\u003e 7141 ms and LU 628 -\u003e 591 ms. Full Python checks (22), Lua checks (17), 19 inliner tests and regular LLVM conformance (43 Lua, 50 Python) pass. However, standard-count sparsematmult warmed iterations regress from about 52 ms to 61 ms, despite its first iteration improving. That regression blocks landing.\n\nPaired inline/HIR traces explain the discontinuity. Inlining zb_number_i64 enlarges zb_any_as_i64 from 16 to 22 instructions, crossing the dispatch threshold of \u003e4 calls and \u003e16 instructions. SparseCompRow_matmult previously inlined the wrapper and then its conversion, but the candidate refuses the enlarged wrapper. Many counted calls are in the wrapper's cold error-message path, ending at cold zb_fatal. HIR text does not print the cold attribute; the attribute is present in source/lowering.\n\nA follow-up guard preserves callers that would cross this threshold. It restores sparsematmult warmed performance (about 53-57 ms) and improves the standard FFT wall median 1243 -\u003e 1168 ms in that paired run, but loses much of the SOR improvement (7922 -\u003e 7661 ms) and regresses Lua op_overload wall 215 -\u003e 234 ms. This variant is also not ready to land.\n\nNow testing whether the dispatch call count should exclude already-classified cold paths while retaining full copied-body/caller instruction budgets and loop-call rejection. This is narrower than the earlier rejected sequential-call-chain heuristic: ordinary error-construction calls without known cold attribution still count.\n\nArtifacts on the NUC: /tmp/zyntax-nuc-scalar-adapter-{speed-all,speed-standard,lua-ab}.json and /tmp/zyntax-nuc-scalar-adapter-refined-{speed-standard,speed-ab,lua-ab}.json. Paired sparse traces/HIR: /tmp/zyntax-scalar-adapter-sparse-{before,after}.{trace,out} and the corresponding -hir directories (also copied locally). Local saved patches: /tmp/zyntax-scalar-adapter-final.patch and /tmp/zyntax-scalar-adapter-preserve-wrapper.patch.","files":null}]}